text:
You are my frontend engineer.

We already have a running backend at:
  http://127.0.0.1:8000

It exposes JSON APIs for MC Tracking:
- GET /subsystems/
- GET /subsystems/{sys_code}/{subsys_code}/tags
- GET /tags/{sys_code}/{subsys_code}/{tag_no}/details
- GET /health

Please transform this new Vite + React + TypeScript project into a fully working MC Tracking frontend.

===========================
TASK 0: Clean template
===========================
- Remove default Vite template code.
- Delete unused assets (logo files, counter components, etc.)
- Create clean structure under src:

src/
  api/
    client.ts
    types.ts
  layout/
    AppLayout.tsx
  pages/
    SubsystemListPage.tsx
    SubsystemDetailPage.tsx
    TagDetailPage.tsx
  router/
    index.tsx
  App.tsx
  main.tsx

===========================
TASK 1: Setup API client
===========================
Create src/api/client.ts:

- axios baseURL = "http://127.0.0.1:8000"
- export axiosInstance
- add simple error logging

Create src/api/types.ts:
- Define TypeScript interfaces:

  Subsystem {
    sys_code: string;
    subsys_code: string;
    name: string | null;
    discipline: string | null;
    tag_total: number;
    mcr_total: number;
    mcr_closed: number;
    tag_with_punch: number;
    progress_pct: number;
    last_update: string | null;
  }

  TagWithStats {
    id: number;
    sys_code: string;
    subsys_code: string;
    tag_no: string;
    description: string | null;
    location: string | null;
    discipline: string | null;
    scope: string | null;
    ref_drawing: string | null;
    mcr_count: number;
    mcr_closed_count: number;
    punch_count: number;
    punch_open_count: number;
  }

  MCItem {
    id: number;
    insp_code: string | null;
    disp: string | null;
    description: string | null;
    scope: string | null;
    location: string | null;
    ref_drawing: string | null;
    complete_date: string | null;
    clear_date: string | null;
    status: string;
  }

  Punch {
    id: number;
    punch_code: string;
    mcr_label: string | null;
    disp: string | null;
    status_code: number | null;
    desc_en: string | null;
    desc_cn: string | null;
    ab_class: string | null;
    punch_date: string | null;
    clear_date: string | null;
    responsible: string | null;
    dept: string | null;
    is_top: string | null;
  }

  TagDetail {
    tag: { ... same fields as TagWithStats but without stats ... };
    mcitems: MCItem[];
    punches: Punch[];
  }

===========================
TASK 2: App layout
===========================
src/layout/AppLayout.tsx:

- Use Ant Design Layout
- Sider with Menu:
    * Dashboard → "/subsystems"
    * Subsystems → "/subsystems"
- Header with title “MC Tracking”

We have validated the database and know the correct global totals:

- The unique TAG count across all subsystems (MCR points) is 36,253.
  This equals SUM(subsystems.tag_total).
- MCR rows total ~38,964 (sum of mcr_total).
- Punches are a subset and do not create new tags.
- The Subsystem overview card in the UI currently shows:
    Total Tags = 6,100 (which is wrong).

Please fix the overview metrics in the Subsystem list page.

File: src/pages/SubsystemListPage.tsx  
(or whichever file renders the "Subsystems Overview" card at the top).

Requirements:

1) We have two pieces of state:
   - `allSubsystems`: the full list loaded from GET /subsystems/
   - `filteredSubsystems`: the list after discipline/progress filters

   If `allSubsystems` is not present yet, please introduce it.

2) Compute the overview metrics ONLY from `allSubsystems`
   (not from the filtered list), so that filters do NOT change
   the overview numbers.

   Use the following formulas:

   ```ts
   const totalTags = allSubsystems.reduce(
     (sum, s) => sum + (s.tag_total ?? 0),
     0
   );

   const totalMcr = allSubsystems.reduce(
     (sum, s) => sum + (s.mcr_total ?? 0),
     0
   );

   const closedMcr = allSubsystems.reduce(
     (sum, s) => sum + (s.mcr_closed ?? 0),
     0
   );

   const mcrClosedPct = totalMcr > 0 ? (closedMcr / totalMcr) * 100 : 0;

   const tagsWithPunch = allSubsystems.reduce(
     (sum, s) => sum + (s.tag_with_punch ?? 0),
     0
   );
